category B changes from 38% to 20%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-17","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["A rose because prices fell.","Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","Both categories rose over the period."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2017–2022: category A changes from 29% to 51%; category B changes from 37% to 20%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-18","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","Both categories rose over the period.","A rose because prices fell."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2018–2023: category A changes from 30% to 52%; category B changes from 36% to 19%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-19","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["Both categories rose over the period.","A rose because prices fell.","Use of A rose, while use of B fell."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2019–2024: category A changes from 31% to 53%; category B changes from 35% to 19%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-20","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["A rose because prices fell.","Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","Both categories rose over the period."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2020–2025: category A changes from 32% to 54%; category B changes from 34% to 18%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-21","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","Both categories rose over the period.","A rose because prices fell."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2021–2026: category A changes from 33% to 55%; category B changes from 33% to 18%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-22","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["Both categories rose over the period.","A rose because prices fell.","Use of A rose, while use of B fell."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2022–2027: category A changes from 34% to 56%; category B changes from 32% to 17%.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"writing_task1_overview-23","kind":"choice","prompt":"Choose an accurate overview of the two changes.","options":["A rose because prices fell.","Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","Both categories rose over the period."],"answer":"Use of A rose, while use of B fell.","explanation":"A increases and B decreases. No reason for either change is provided.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Travel survey 2023–2028: category A changes from 35% to 57%; category B changes from 31% to 17%.","stage":"independent"}]}'::jsonb,true) on conflict(skill,version) do nothing;
insert into skill_lab_private.lessons(skill,module,version,content,published) values ('speaking_answer_extension','speaking',1,'{"skill":"speaking_answer_extension","module":"speaking","title":"Extend a relevant answer","outcome":"Add a reason and a relevant detail to a direct answer.","trap":"Speaking longer is not useful when the answer goes off topic.","strategy":"Answer directly, explain why, then add one relevant example.","example":"Do you use libraries? Yes, because I need a quiet place. I usually read there after work.","version":1,"basic":true,"estimated_minutes":8,"open_prompt":"Practise extend a relevant answer. Describe a useful local service. Give a relevant reason and example.","items":[{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-0","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["People who work during the day can then borrow books after work.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"People who work during the day can then borrow books after work.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A nurse finishing at six could visit at seven.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Public libraries should offer evening hours.","stage":"guided"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Separating bicycles from cars can make the journey safer."],"answer":"Separating bicycles from cars can make the journey safer.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A physical barrier keeps turning vehicles out of the cycle lane.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Cities should protect cycle lanes.","stage":"guided"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","An uninterrupted period helps students focus on a text.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"An uninterrupted period helps students focus on a text.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A class could read for fifteen minutes before discussing the story.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Schools should provide quiet reading time.","stage":"guided"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Shade gives visitors a place to rest during hot weather.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Shade gives visitors a place to rest during hot weather.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Older walkers could pause under a tree rather than leave early.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Parks need shaded seating.","stage":"guided"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-4","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Some workers can avoid the busiest commuting period."],"answer":"Some workers can avoid the busiest commuting period.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Starting at ten instead of nine may allow a less crowded train journey.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Employers should allow flexible start times.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-5","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Visitors need context to understand unfamiliar objects.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Visitors need context to understand unfamiliar objects.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A date and short description can explain how a tool was used.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Museums should label exhibits clearly.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-6","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Students often manage rent and food costs for the first time.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Students often manage rent and food costs for the first time.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A monthly spending exercise can reveal whether rent leaves enough for meals.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Universities should teach basic budgeting.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-7","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Returning containers can reduce disposable packaging."],"answer":"Returning containers can reduce disposable packaging.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A vegetable seller could refill the same crate each week.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Local markets should provide reusable crates.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-8","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Visitors can find services without asking for directions.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Visitors can find services without asking for directions.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A large reception sign helps a first-time visitor identify the right desk.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Public buildings need clear signs.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-9","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Experiments connect an abstract explanation to an observable result.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Experiments connect an abstract explanation to an observable result.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Watching ice melt lets pupils examine a change of state.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Schools should include practical science.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-10","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","An even surface makes short journeys more accessible."],"answer":"An even surface makes short journeys more accessible.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Repairing a broken pavement helps a person using a walking frame.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Towns should maintain walking paths.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-11","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Sharing reduces the need to buy rarely used items.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Sharing reduces the need to buy rarely used items.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Residents could borrow a projector for an occasional meeting.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Community centres should lend equipment.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-12","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Some tasks require sustained concentration.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Some tasks require sustained concentration.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: An analyst could check a report away from telephone conversations.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Offices should provide quiet rooms.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-13","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Simple recipes help students prepare meals independently."],"answer":"Simple recipes help students prepare meals independently.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A student who can cook rice and vegetables has an affordable dinner option.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Schools should teach cooking skills.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-14","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Knowing the expected wait helps passengers plan their journey.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Knowing the expected wait helps passengers plan their journey.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A passenger can decide whether there is time to buy water nearby.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Bus stops should display arrival times.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-15","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["New participants may need slower instruction before joining experienced players.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"New participants may need slower instruction before joining experienced players.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A first-time player can practise serving before playing a match.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Sports clubs should offer beginner sessions.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-16","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Preventing losses preserves treated water."],"answer":"Preventing losses preserves treated water.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Fixing a street leak keeps water in the supply network.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Councils should repair leaking pipes.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-17","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Readers can borrow without travelling to a branch.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Readers can borrow without travelling to a branch.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Someone recovering at home could download a novel.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Libraries should lend digital books.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-18","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Training reduces confusion when familiar procedures change.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Training reduces confusion when familiar procedures change.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A short demonstration can show staff where to save a shared document.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Workplaces should explain new software.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-19","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","Coordinated work can cover a larger area."],"answer":"Coordinated work can cover a larger area.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Small teams can clean separate streets on the same morning.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Neighbourhoods should organise litter collections.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-20","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Growing plants helps pupils observe how food develops.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Growing plants helps pupils observe how food develops.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Measuring a bean plant each week records its growth.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Schools should maintain vegetable gardens.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-21","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["Shelter makes waiting more comfortable in poor weather.","This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world."],"answer":"Shelter makes waiting more comfortable in poor weather.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: Passengers can stay dry during a rain shower.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Stations should provide covered waiting areas.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-22","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["This is an important issue and it is very important.","There are many different things in the world.","A reminder helps patients remember a booking made weeks earlier."],"answer":"A reminder helps patients remember a booking made weeks earlier.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: A message the previous day gives time to arrange transport.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Clinics should send appointment reminders.","stage":"independent"},{"id":"speaking_answer_extension-23","kind":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence best develops this idea?","options":["There are many different things in the world.","Discussion lets learners compare explanations of difficult material.","This is an important issue and it is very important."],"answer":"Discussion lets learners compare explanations of difficult material.","explanation":"The reason explains the claim directly. A useful supporting example is: One student can explain a worked example while another checks the reasoning.","hint":"Compare every detail with the lesson strategy.","passage":"Universities should provide study groups.","stage":"independent"}]}'::jsonb,true) on conflict(skill,version) do nothing;
insert into skill_lab_private.lessons(skill,module,version,content,published) values ('speaking_organisation','speaking',1,'{"skill":"speaking_organisation","module":"speaking","title":"Organise a longer answer","outcome":"Give your listener an easy sequence to follow.","trap":"Memorised connectors cannot replace a clear sequence.","strategy":"Introduce the subject, explain the reason or sequence, and finish with a relevant detail.","example":"Describe a useful service: name it → explain its use → give a personal example.","version":1,"basic":true,"estimated_minutes":8,"open_prompt":"Practise organise a longer answer. Describe a useful local service. Give a relevant reason and example.","items":[{"id":"speaking_organisation-0","kind":"order","prompt":"Put the claim, reason and example in a logical order.","options":["A nurse finishing at six could visit at seven.","Public libraries should offer evening hours.","People who work during the day can then borrow books after work."],"answer":["Public libraries should offer evening hours.","People who work during the day can then borrow books after work.","A nurse finishing at six could visit at seven."],"explanation":"The claim introduces the subject. The reason explains it. The example illustrates that reason.","hint":"Introduce the idea before explaining or illustrating it.","stage":"guided"},{"id":"speaking_organisation-1","kind":"order","prompt":"Put the claim, reason and example in a logical order.","options":["A physical barrier keeps turning vehicles out of the cycle lane.","Cities should protect cycle lanes.","Separating bicycles from cars can make the journey safer."],"answer":["Cities should protect cycle lanes.","Separating bicycles from cars can make the journey safer.","A physical barrier keeps turning vehicles out of the cycle lane."],"explanation":"The claim introduces the subject. The reason explains it. The example illustrates that reason.","hint":"Introduce the idea before explaining or illustrating it."